license.copyright.title=Copyright
license.tldr.title=Quick TL;DR for non-lawyers (not legally binding)
license.tldr.private=You can fork, modify, and use the app privately as much as you like. If you only use your changes privately and do not share the modified app, you do not have to publish or share your code/your derivative work.
license.tldr.source=If you share a modified version of the app, you must make its complete corresponding source code available to the recipients under GPLv3. This does not mean you have to publish it publicly on the internet.
license.tldr.commercial=GPLv3 permits commercial use and even charging for copies, as long as you follow its terms.
license.thirdparty=Third-party components and artwork remain subject to their own licenses; see THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md or open the Contributions tab within the app to view each specific license directly.
license.tldr.derivative=If you incorporate GPLv3-covered code into another program and distribute the resulting derivative work, you must make the complete corresponding source code of that work available under GPLv3 — not just the parts copied from this app. This does not automatically apply to independent programs merely used alongside it.
license.tldr.reference=For a more detailed explanation, see {0}'s take on this topic.
license.purpose=I basically want to keep the app freely available, retain my copyright, and prevent anyone — especially large corporations — from just taking the code into a proprietary derivative without respecting the GPL (aka stealing the work for themselves). Commercial use is still allowed under GPLv3 terms.
license.explore=From a technical perspective, I also want to give people free and unobfuscated access to the code. You might be learning to program, exploring process inspection, or searching for a solution to a specific problem. Why not let people look around? That is how we grow.
license.audit=And when software has security-relevant features, such as transport encryption, being able to audit the code is a very legitimate interest!
pro.headline=Hahaha - got you!!
pro.intro=This app is totally free (see the License tab) and there is no Pro version.{0}Everything is already fully unlocked!!
pro.why.title=Why is that?
pro.why.body=Well, I believe you are a nice person.{0}If this app serves you well, send me an amount of your choosing -
pro.why.body.italic=just because you are a good person and it's the right thing to do.
pro.doubt.title=Don't believe me? “Why would you do that?”
pro.doubt.body=Distributing the app this way lets people who are worse off financially (or live in a country where a euro or dollar is much more expensive for them) use it too. I especially don't want anyone to have to jump through hoops just to plead for a free license somewhere. How annoying and degrading is that?
pro.serious.title=No, seriously:
pro.serious.body1=We need to bring back a bit of good in this world, and for me that starts with making this app universally accessible, whatever your circumstances.
pro.serious.body2.before=For you, that can mean getting a big grin on your face and simply using the app as it is,
pro.serious.body2.italic=without paying a dime
pro.serious.body2.after=.
pro.serious.closing=Neither choice is right or wrong.
